      "word": "ENNOBLE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To make noble; to elevate in degree, qualities, or excellence; to dignify. \"Ennobling all that he touches.\" Trench. What can ennoble sots, or slaves, or cowards Alas! not all the blood of all the Howards. Pope.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To raise to the rank of nobility; as, to ennoble a commoner.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
